## Priority Queue with Interfaces

### The Comparable Constraint

```xiom
interface Priority {
  fn is_higher_than(&self, other: &Self) -> Bool;
}
```

### The Priority Queue

```xiom
type PriorityQueue[T: Priority] {
  items: Vec[T];
}

fn PriorityQueue.insert[T: Priority](&mut self, item: T) {
  // Find the right position to maintain order
  let mut pos = 0;
  while pos < self.items.len() {
    if item.is_higher_than(self.items.get(pos).unwrap()) {
      break;
    };
    pos += 1;
  };
  self.items.insert(pos, item);
}

fn PriorityQueue.pop[T: Priority](&mut self) -> Option[T] {
  if self.items.len() == 0 {
    return Option.None;
  };
  let last = self.items.len() - 1;
  let result = self.items.get(last).unwrap().clone();
  self.items.remove(last);
  Option.Some(result)
}
```

Items are inserted in priority order. `pop()` always removes the highest-priority item (last in the Vec).

### Implementing Priority

```xiom
type Patient { name: Str; severity: Int; }

fn Patient.is_higher_than(&self, other: &Patient) -> Bool {
  self.severity > other.severity
}
```

